{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1470419-aeon-what-s-going-on-on-venus","id":1470419,"title":"[AEON] What's going on on Venus?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-14T04:34:39-08:00","id":1470419,"title":"[AEON] What's going on on Venus?","content":"Or rather: is anything going on there at all?<br /> In Aeon, the colonisation of our home solar system had fallen behind somewhat, because thanks to the possibility of interstellar space travel, humanity could more or less cherry-pick planets that could be colonised. That is why the population of Mars at the beginning of the 22nd century is comparatively low.<br /> Now Mars, asteroids and the moons of the outer planets are not the only worthwhile targets. There is also Venus! And it does indeed offer some potential! Here are a few interesting YouTube videos on the subject:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l7A0O_4J5LE\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l7A0O_4J5LE\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l7A0O_4J5LE\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l7A0O_4J5LE </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gJ5KV3rzuag\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gJ5KV3rzuag\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gJ5KV3rzuag\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gJ5KV3rzuag </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uCYyog_CD_c\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uCYyog_CD_c\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uCYyog_CD_c\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uCYyog_CD_c </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> This raises the question of what the colonisation of Venus looks like in Aeon. Is there any more detailed material on this somewhere? And if not: What could be settled on Venus? Are there a few lonely research stations floating high above the surface? Are there cloud cities with several thousand inhabitants? Or is Venus, apart from a few scientific missions, simply still completely untouched?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","name":"Waldi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T07:50:45-08:00","id":1470434,"title":"","content":"I certainly imagine that several entities have put aerostats on Venus. I also imagine it's an ideal place for old Aberrants to live in peace away from Earth, but not too far away!<br /> For a really cool look at what a colonized Venus might look like, I'd look at the Morningstar Constellation in the RPG Eclipse Phase, an independent nation of aerostat city states that make money from mining the surface with telepresence-controlled robots and from tourism and casinos.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://robboyle.wordpress.com/eclipse-phase-pdfs/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://robboyle.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2010/05/eclipsephase_cover_phs.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://robboyle.wordpress.com/eclipse-phase-pdfs/\" target=\"_blank\"> Eclipse Phase PDFs </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://robboyle.wordpress.com/eclipse-phase-pdfs/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://robboyle.wordpress.com/eclipse-phase-pdfs/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Many thanks to everyone who contributed to the Kickstarter for Eclipse Phase, Second Edition! The Eclipse Phase roleplaying game is released under a Creative Commons license. To facilitate access t&hellip; </div> </div> </div><br /> (It's under a Creative Commons Agreement and is legal to share. Sunward, pg. 24 has details)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T11:43:32-08:00","id":1470457,"title":"","content":"Thanks! \ud83d\ude00 Adapting ideas from Eclipse Phase I think is a great idea! For example, the exurgents on the surface of Venus could be excellently replaced by aberrants. Also, the technology used to build the colonies and some of the peculiarities of life on Venus could be adopted quite excellently. AEON is a little less extreme than Eclipse Phase when it comes to transhumanism, but that doesn't affect colony construction. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","name":"Waldi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T13:35:38-08:00","id":1470466,"title":"","content":"Venus would be a fantastic for colonization. Assuming you could deal with its atmosphere first. I've always liked the idea of a terraformed Venus because honestly if humans could do that it would be way more ideal than Mars as a human colony. For Aeon, I'd think the limiting factor would be cost and lack of appropriate tech. Novas working together I'm sure could do it, but without them it would likely be a very very costly and difficult mission. There is mention of new terraforming tech gifted by the Qin but that strikes me as more for creating ecosystems than altering facets of a planet like one as dense, poisonous, and hot as that. An interesting story hook maybe is that an old Daedalus League technology that was meant to spend decades altering a the planet's atmosphere has had results that recent scientists have noticed and hope to exploit. You could make a story out of investigating, making sure there aren't unknown dangers from the technology or monstrous subaberrant mutants that are there. Or they could stumble upon a silicon based life form that requires the ultra dense carbon dioxide atmosphere to breath and the changing atmosphere is killing them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T14:01:17-08:00","id":1470470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Waldi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1470419-aeon-what-s-going-on-on-venus?p=1470457#post1470457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks! \ud83d\ude00 Adapting ideas from Eclipse Phase I think is a great idea! For example, the exurgents on the surface of Venus could be excellently replaced by aberrants. Also, the technology used to build the colonies and some of the peculiarities of life on Venus could be adopted quite excellently. AEON is a little less extreme than Eclipse Phase when it comes to transhumanism, but that doesn't affect colony construction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually have used the the Exsurgent Virus as inspiration for a Quantum-powered Alien Type II civilization for Novas to fight, and provide a disturbing image for what they might eventually turn into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T14:03:51-08:00","id":1470472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1470419-aeon-what-s-going-on-on-venus?p=1470466#post1470466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Venus would be a fantastic for colonization. Assuming you could deal with its atmosphere first. I've always liked the idea of a terraformed Venus because honestly if humans could do that it would be way more ideal than Mars as a human colony. For Aeon, I'd think the limiting factor would be cost and lack of appropriate tech. Novas working together I'm sure could do it, but without them it would likely be a very very costly and difficult mission. There is mention of new terraforming tech gifted by the Qin but that strikes me as more for creating ecosystems than altering facets of a planet like one as dense, poisonous, and hot as that. An interesting story hook maybe is that an old Daedalus League technology that was meant to spend decades altering a the planet's atmosphere has had results that recent scientists have noticed and hope to exploit. You could make a story out of investigating, making sure there aren't unknown dangers from the technology or monstrous subaberrant mutants that are there. Or they could stumble upon a silicon based life form that requires the ultra dense carbon dioxide atmosphere to breath and the changing atmosphere is killing them</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of the colonization ideas for Venus that Waldi posted actually involve not terraforming the planet at all, but adapting aerostats and humans to live in the clouds, where the atmosphere is less toxic, not acidic and has a much milder temperature and pressure. It'd be easily with the capability of Aeon-era humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T15:12:47-08:00","id":1470480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Waldi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1470419-aeon-what-s-going-on-on-venus#post1470419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or rather: is anything going on there at all?<br /> In Aeon, the colonisation of our home solar system had fallen behind somewhat, because thanks to the possibility of interstellar space travel, humanity could more or less cherry-pick planets that could be colonised. That is why the population of Mars at the beginning of the 22nd century is comparatively low.<br /> Now Mars, asteroids and the moons of the outer planets are not the only worthwhile targets. There is also Venus! And it does indeed offer some potential! Here are a few interesting YouTube videos on the subject:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l7A0O_4J5LE\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l7A0O_4J5LE\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l7A0O_4J5LE\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l7A0O_4J5LE </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gJ5KV3rzuag\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gJ5KV3rzuag\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gJ5KV3rzuag\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gJ5KV3rzuag </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uCYyog_CD_c\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uCYyog_CD_c\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uCYyog_CD_c\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uCYyog_CD_c </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> This raises the question of what the colonisation of Venus looks like in Aeon. Is there any more detailed material on this somewhere? And if not: What could be settled on Venus? Are there a few lonely research stations floating high above the surface? Are there cloud cities with several thousand inhabitants? Or is Venus, apart from a few scientific missions, simply still completely untouched?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the biggest reason that Venus hasn't been colonized in Aeon is similar to why it hasn't been colonized in the Expanse or our own reality. Venus is an unlivable toxic hell-world. In the timelines of both Aberrant and Aeon there's other places that are way more hospitable to humans than Venus that became accessible through Quantum or Psionic teleportation. Meanwhile is their anything on Venus that humans would want that would be worth going their to get? Probably not much.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T01:09:23-08:00","id":1470514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Waldi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1470419-aeon-what-s-going-on-on-venus#post1470419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l7A0O_4J5LE\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l7A0O_4J5LE\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l7A0O_4J5LE\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l7A0O_4J5LE </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gJ5KV3rzuag\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gJ5KV3rzuag\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gJ5KV3rzuag\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gJ5KV3rzuag </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uCYyog_CD_c\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uCYyog_CD_c</a></div> </div> </div> </div><b>In a Nutshell</b> made 'easy to understand' video on how to terraform Venus <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G-WO-z-QuWI\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G-WO-z-QuWI\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G-WO-z-QuWI\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G-WO-z-QuWI </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ( I generally advise this channel, as it's great for popular science content )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T12:35:51-08:00","id":1470547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Waldi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1470419-aeon-what-s-going-on-on-venus#post1470419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This raises the question of what the colonisation of Venus looks like in Aeon.</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s plenty going on with Venus, but colonisation probably isn\u2019t any kind of focus. Scientific habitats and manufacturing facilities in orbit take advantage of Venus\u2019 conditions. The Norca are the main group working on the surface, as BK makes survival possible (even easy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T16:14:23-08:00","id":1470559,"title":"","content":"Seeding the upper clouds of Venus with life forms that slowly terraform the planet would be a thing. An automated aerostat, long abandoned by humanity, would make a great &quot;haunted house&quot; setting. <br /> <br /> The very size that would be required for aerostats would fit the haunted house genre (either haunted with ghosts, memories, or human failings). Small houses rarely get ghost stories, ghosts seem to need large amounts of room to haunt. So we humans place our ghosts in big mostly empty buildings. An empty aerostat would attract ghost stories just like any other large abandoned structure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T05:23:16-08:00","id":1470704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1470419-aeon-what-s-going-on-on-venus?p=1470559#post1470559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeding the upper clouds of Venus with life forms that slowly terraform the planet would be a thing. An automated aerostat, long abandoned by humanity, would make a great &quot;haunted house&quot; setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is indeed an awesome idea! Except that the environment is not made up of claustrophobic, metal corridors, but in part of narrow gangways, floating platforms and gauzy eufiber tarpaulin. An aerostat is more or less a stationary zeppelin and not a massive space station. Therefore, the whole installation could be characterised by an extremely lightweight construction.And instead of triggering the characters with their claustrophobia, as is usual in space horror, you trigger them with their fear of heights. Only a wafer-thin membrane separates them from the toxic Venusian atmosphere, below them is nothing but a void of swirling clouds and with every gust of wind the entire facility groans and creaks. Ooooh yes...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","name":"Waldi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T08:41:20-08:00","id":1471014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Waldi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1470419-aeon-what-s-going-on-on-venus?p=1470704#post1470704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is indeed an awesome idea! Except that the environment is not made up of claustrophobic, metal corridors, but in part of narrow gangways, floating platforms and gauzy eufiber tarpaulin. An aerostat is more or less a stationary zeppelin and not a massive space station. Therefore, the whole installation could be characterised by an extremely lightweight construction.And instead of triggering the characters with their claustrophobia, as is usual in space horror, you trigger them with their fear of heights. Only a wafer-thin membrane separates them from the toxic Venusian atmosphere, below them is nothing but a void of swirling clouds and with every gust of wind the entire facility groans and creaks. Ooooh yes...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In the words of Mrs. Lovitt &quot;Good you got it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Like the movie Suspiria(1977), a haunted house story set on Venus mines the disorienting power of the radically different esthetic.<br /> <br /> Minor bonus, the size of the aerostats means that, if the aerostat isn't carefully maintained, there will be weather in them. Mists, fogs, occasional rain, even a rare dust devil or two. The mist would be the most common phenomena, as well as the most subtly creepy one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 12-21-2021, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-22T04:36:37-08:00","id":1471077,"title":"","content":"Oh, thats awesome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Now add some spook, that is probably telepathic in nature. So, no drooling aliens munching on peoples intestines this time. Instead, the haunted aerostat is filled with dreamlike psychedelic visions, strange voices in the mist and formless shadows lurking in the clouds beneath the station. Maybe, some wealthy Telepaths, who were interested in european spiritism, conducted some experiments there, with the help of cutting edge PSI-boosting biotech...then something went wrong...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","name":"Waldi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}